cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DESQ: Dynamic-Flooding Transformer Ensembles for Reinforcement-Learning-Based Equity Market Timing"
message: "If you use this software or the reviewer reproducibility kit, please cite the specific release DOI (see below) rather than the head of the main branch."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Tung-Li"
    family-names: "Chen"
    affiliation: "National Taiwan University"
    # Add ORCID once available; changes are non-breaking for the DOI record.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tunglich/DESQ"
license: MIT
version: "1.1-desq"
date-released: "2026-08-29"
# The DOI below is minted automatically by Zenodo when the v1.1-desq release
# is published on GitHub. Replace <TO_BE_ASSIGNED_BY_ZENODO> with the string
# Zenodo prints (e.g. "10.5281/zenodo.1234567") in the follow-up commit; the
# release itself is immutable so the citation remains valid.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "<TO_BE_ASSIGNED_BY_ZENODO>"
    description: "Concept + version DOI for the v1.1-desq revised-paper release."
keywords:
  - dynamic-ensemble-selection
  - deslib
  - quantitative-finance
  - reproducible-research
  - stock-selection
  - tw50
abstract: >-
  DESQ is the reference implementation of the revised IEEE Access paper's
  four-stage market-timing framework: attention specialists, Dynamic
  Flooding, KNORA-E dynamic ensemble selection, and Signal-Conditioned
  Double DQN. The v1.1-desq release adds canonical Tables 3-10 with explicit
  evidence status, five paper-defined walk-forward windows, the 50-anchor
  effective gap, paper-aligned trading costs, and Appendix F monitoring
  governance. Legacy DES/CUSUM outputs remain clearly labeled diagnostics.
